# HR feature vertical slices (`@afenda/feature-hr-suite`)

**ARCH-010** (HR package) · **ARCH-002** · **ARCH-008**. Reference implementation: `@afenda/feature-system-admin` (rule `afenda-system-admin`).

## Shipped capability layout

Each **implemented** capability lives under `src/<category>/<capability-slug>/` with standard buckets:

```txt
compliance-regulatory-tracking/
  actions/       # *.actions.server.ts ("use server")
  components/    # *.component.client.tsx
  contracts/     # permission / DTO contracts
  data/          # queries, page models, *.shared.ts — not list surfaces
  events/        # audit action strings, domain events
  policies/      # *-access.policy.server.ts capability guards
  schemas/       # Zod
  surface/       # *.surface.ts, *-ui.copy.shared.ts
  server.ts      # slice server door (barrel + server chrome)
  client.ts      # slice client door (components only)
  metadata.ts    # slice metadata door (surfaces + copy only)
  index.ts       # neutral door (metadata + client + contracts)
  *-architecture.md
```

Scaffold-only capabilities may keep placeholder buckets until a TRACK-004 slice ships.

## HR Suite root discipline

`src/` may contain only package public doors, HR category folders, and `hr-suite-integration/`.

Allowed HR category folders:

- `employee-management/`
- `industry-specific/`
- `payroll-compensation/`
- `talent-management/`
- `time-attendance/`

Forbidden at HR Suite root: `actions/`, `components/`, `contracts/`, `data/`, `events/`, `navigation/`, `policies/`, `schemas/`, `surface/`, `tests/`.

Suite-level glue belongs in `src/hr-suite-integration/`. It must expose exactly four root doors:

- `index.ts` — environment-neutral constants/types only
- `client.ts` — client components only
- `server.ts` — server-only guards/actions only
- `metadata.ts` — metadata-safe navigation/surface exports only

Consumers must import only these doors. Do not deep-import `hr-suite-integration/components`, `hr-suite-integration/contracts`, `hr-suite-integration/navigation`, or `hr-suite-integration/policies` from outside `hr-suite-integration`.

## File naming (mirrors system-admin)

Prefix: **`hr.<domain>.`** where `<domain>` matches governed surface keys (e.g. `hr.workforce.compliance` → keys `hr.workforce.compliance.obligations.list`).

| Role | Pattern | Example |
| ---- | ------- | ------- |
| Actions | `hr.<domain>.actions.server.ts` | `hr.workforce.compliance.actions.server.ts` |
| Policy | `hr.<domain>-access.policy.server.ts` | `hr.workforce.compliance-access.policy.server.ts` |
| Page model | `hr.<domain>.page-model.server.ts` | `hr.workforce.compliance.page-model.server.ts` |
| List surface | `hr.<domain>-<purpose>-list.surface.ts` | `hr.workforce.compliance-obligations-list.surface.ts` |
| UI copy | `hr.<domain>-ui.copy.shared.ts` | `hr.workforce.compliance-ui.copy.shared.ts` |
| Shared logic | `hr.<domain>-<topic>.shared.ts` | `hr.workforce.compliance-obligation.shared.ts` |
| Schema | `hr.<domain>-<topic>.schema.ts` | `hr.workforce.compliance-obligation.schema.ts` |
| Contract | `hr.<domain>.contract.ts` | `hr.workforce.compliance.contract.ts` |
| Events / audit | `hr.<domain>.event.ts` | `hr.workforce.compliance.event.ts` |
| Component | `hr.<domain>-<purpose>.component.client.tsx` | `hr.workforce.compliance-forms.component.client.tsx` |

## Export doors

| Door | May export |
| ---- | ---------- |
| `./server` | actions, data, policies, events, schemas, contracts, server chrome |
| `./client` | client components and client-safe catalogs only |
| `./metadata` | surface builders, surface keys, UI copy — **no tenant I/O** |

Do not export list surfaces from `./server`. Do not export server actions from `./client`.

## Capabilities & audit

- Capability keys: `hr.<area>.read|write` (e.g. `hr.compliance.read`).
- Audit strings: `hr.<area>.<entity>.<verb>` — define in `events/*.event.ts`, not contracts.
- Mutations: `writeExecutionAuditEvent` + `revalidatePath` for the owning HR route.

## Verification

```bash
pnpm exec tsx packages/features/hr-suite/scripts/check-hr-feature-vertical-naming.mts
pnpm --filter @afenda/feature-hr-suite typecheck
pnpm --filter @afenda/feature-hr-suite test
pnpm architecture:check
pnpm lint:governed-renderers   # when surfaces change
```

Guard runs in `pnpm architecture:check` and via `validate-feature-shape` hooks on edit.
